# No AI eyebrow type

Do not style labels, kickers, badges, or status text as tiny tracked-out caps. That look is banned on this site.

Never combine these (or close variants):

- `uppercase`
- wide tracking (`tracking-wide`, `tracking-widest`, `tracking-[0.1em]` or looser)
- micro type (`text-[9px]`, `text-[10px]`, `text-[11px]`, `text-xs` used as a section kicker)
- `font-mono` used as a UI label or kicker

```tsx
// BAD
<p className="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] text-ticket uppercase">
  Open now
</p>

// GOOD
<p className="text-base font-medium text-ticket">Open now</p>
```

Write labels in sentence case at `text-sm` or `text-base`. Use the same fonts as surrounding copy. Times, prices, and stall numbers use `type-nums` — Mona semibold condensed, not a coding mono. Directory counts on the ticket use `type-census` (Barlow Condensed ExtraBold).

Status chips (open now, selling now) may use the ticket plate color. They still read as normal words: `Open now`, not `OPEN NOW`.
